            <ArticleTitle>Delivery related rupture of the gravid uterus: imaging findings.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>120-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Rupture of the gravid uterus is a rare, life-threatening obstetric complication. Major symptoms are hypovolemic shock and abdominal pain during late pregnancy or after vaginal delivery. Immediate surgical therapy is required. We report a case of uterine rupture after vaginal delivery diagnosed by means of ultrasonography and computed tomography.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
